---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const title = 'Privacy Policy | Modus Data GmbH';
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description="Privacy policy for Modus Data GmbH and its website visitors.">
  <article class="markdown-content legal-page">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>

    <p>
      Modus Data GmbH takes data protection seriously. This privacy policy explains how we process personal
      data when you visit our website or contact us.
    </p>

    <h2>Who is responsible?</h2>
    <p>
      Modus Data GmbH<br />
      Therwil / Basel, Switzerland<br />
      Email: <a href="mailto:arthur@modusdata.ch">arthur@modusdata.ch</a>
    </p>

    <h2>Personal data we may process</h2>
    <p>
      When you contact us, subscribe to a service, or engage in a business relationship, we may process
      personal data such as your name, company, email address, phone number, communication history, and
      project-related information necessary for the purpose of the engagement.
    </p>

    <h2>Purposes of processing</h2>
    <p>We process personal data for the following purposes:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>responding to inquiries and requests</li>
      <li>managing client and project relationships</li>
      <li>providing consulting, engineering, and AI implementation services</li>
      <li>fulfilling legal, accounting, and contractual obligations</li>
      <li>maintaining the security and integrity of our website and systems</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Legal basis</h2>
    <p>
      We process personal data on the basis of legitimate interest, contract performance, compliance with
      legal obligations, and, where applicable, your consent. In some cases, Swiss and European data
      protection rules may also require us to provide additional information or to honor specific rights.
    </p>

    <h2>Data retention</h2>
    <p>
      We keep personal data only as long as necessary for the stated purpose, legal obligations, or the
      duration of a contractual relationship. Once the need has passed, we delete or anonymize the data
      unless retention is required by law.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>Depending on the applicable law, you may have the right to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>request access to your personal data</li>
      <li>request correction or deletion</li>
      <li>object to certain processing activities</li>
      <li>request restriction of processing</li>
      <li>request data portability where technically feasible</li>
      <li>withdraw consent where consent was used as the legal basis</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      If you wish to exercise any of these rights, please contact us at
      <a href="mailto:arthur@modusdata.ch">arthur@modusdata.ch</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies and analytics</h2>
    <p>
      With your prior consent, this website uses the LinkedIn Insight Tag provided by LinkedIn Ireland
      Unlimited Company. It helps us understand visits from LinkedIn and measure the effectiveness of our
      campaigns. LinkedIn may process technical information such as IP address, browser and device data,
      page visits, and interaction data. LinkedIn may set or read cookies or use similar technologies for
      this purpose. The tag is not loaded unless you select “Allow analytics” in the consent notice.
    </p>
    <p>
      You can decline analytics when the notice appears. To withdraw consent later, clear this site’s
      local storage and reload the page, or contact us at
      <a href="mailto:arthur@modusdata.ch">arthur@modusdata.ch</a>. For more information, see
      <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/legal/privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">LinkedIn’s Privacy Policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this policy from time to time to reflect operational changes or legal requirements. The
      latest version will always be published on this page.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
